  ('20000001-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 2, 'Which agency licenses cosmetologists in California?', 'Board of Barbering and Cosmetology (BBC)', 'U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA)', 'Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)', 'Federal Trade Commission (FTC)', 'A', 'Board of Barbering and Cosmetology (BBC) regulates cosmetology licensure in California.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 5),
  ('20000002-4000-8000-000000000002'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'How many clock hours of training are required for a California cosmetology operator license (current rule)?', '1600 hours', '1000 hours', '1200 hours', '1000 hours', 'A', 'California requires 1600 training hours for the cosmetology pathway cited in California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 5),
  ('20000003-4000-8000-000000000003'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'Who administers the California cosmetology written examination (typical vendor)?', 'Pearson VUE / National Testing Network', 'Internal school-only exams with no outside vendor', 'County health departments only', 'U.S. Department of Education directly', 'A', 'Candidates in California schedule through Pearson VUE / National Testing Network unless the board publishes a change—verify https://www.barberingcosmetology.ca.gov/.', 'https://www.barberingcosmetology.ca.gov/', 5),
  ('20000004-4000-8000-000000000004'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'What is the minimum passing score on the California cosmetology written exam (published target)?', '75%', '50%', '90%', '100% — any missed question fails', 'A', 'California sets a passing standard of 75% on the written portion for this license class.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 5),
  ('20000005-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'flashcard', 'state_law', 3, 'In California, cosmetology rules are found in California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'true', 'State law for California cosmetology is anchored in California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 4),
  ('20000006-4000-8000-000000000006'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'flashcard', 'state_law', 3, 'A California cosmetology candidate may ignore Board of Barbering and Cosmetology (BBC) sanitation rules if their salon has private insurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'Licensure and inspection standards from Board of Barbering and Cosmetology (BBC) apply regardless of private insurance.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 4),
  ('20000007-4000-8000-000000000007'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 3, 'After a California salon service, multi-use metal implements must be:', 'Cleaned, then disinfected per EPA-registered label instructions', 'Rinsed in plain water only', 'Wiped with a dry towel only', 'Stored without cleaning until the next client', 'A', 'Board of Barbering and Cosmetology (BBC) expects infection control consistent with California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10 and CDC best practices.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 5),
  ('20000008-4000-8000-000000000008'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 4, 'Blood on a workstation during a California service requires:', 'Stop service, glove up, clean with appropriate bloodborne pathogen protocol', 'Continue service if the client says it is fine', 'Cover with a cape and proceed', 'Wait until closing to disinfect', 'A', 'Bloodborne exposure procedures are enforced under California cosmetology sanitation rules.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 5),
  ('20000009-4000-8000-000000000009'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'true_false', 'sanitation', 3, 'Single-use porous items in California salons may be reused if they look clean.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'Porous single-use supplies must be discarded after one client.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 4),
  ('20000010-4000-8000-000000000010'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'anatomy', 2, 'The outermost layer of skin primarily responsible for barrier protection is the:', 'Epidermis', 'Dermis', 'Subcutaneous tissue', 'Matrix', 'A', 'Epidermis is the protective outer layer tested on national and state theory exams.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Skin Structure', 4),
  ('20000011-4000-8000-000000000011'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'anatomy', 2, 'Hair grows from the:', 'Hair follicle / dermal papilla', 'Epidermis only', 'Stratum corneum', 'Arrector pili exclusively', 'A', 'Active growth originates in the follicle at the dermal papilla.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Hair Structure', 4),
  ('20000012-4000-8000-000000000012'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'chemistry', 3, 'On the level system, level 7 represents:', 'Medium blonde depth', 'Black', 'Lightest blonde only', 'Red only', 'A', 'Level 7 is medium blonde on the 1–10 depth scale.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Haircolor', 4),
  ('20000013-4000-8000-000000000013'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'chemistry', 3, '20-volume developer is commonly used in California salons to:', 'Deposit on previously colored hair and lift up to ~2 levels on virgin hair', 'Guarantee 5 levels of lift on every scalp application', 'Replace disinfectant solutions', 'Neutralize relaxers without testing', 'A', '20-volume is standard deposit/slight-lift developer; always follow manufacturer and state scope.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 4),
  ('20000014-4000-8000-000000000014'::uuid, 'e2000001-0002-4002-8002-000000000002'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'practical', 3, 'Before chemical services in California, a required safety step is:', 'Consultation and patch test when manufacturer or state rules require', 'Skipping consultation for returning clients', 'Applying highest volume developer first', 'Mixing unrelated brands for speed', 'A', 'Board of Barbering and Cosmetology (BBC) expects documented consultations; patch tests protect clients and licensees.', 'California Business and Professions Code, Division 3, Chapter 10', 5),
