  ('30000001-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 2, 'Which agency licenses cosmetologists in Florida?', 'Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation (DBPR), Board of Cosmetology', 'U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA)', 'Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)', 'Federal Trade Commission (FTC)', 'A', 'Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation (DBPR), Board of Cosmetology regulates cosmetology licensure in Florida.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 5),
  ('30000002-4000-8000-000000000002'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'How many clock hours of training are required for a Florida cosmetology operator license (current rule)?', '1200 hours', '1000 hours', '1600 hours', '1000 hours', 'A', 'Florida requires 1200 training hours for the cosmetology pathway cited in Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 5),
  ('30000003-4000-8000-000000000003'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'Who administers the Florida cosmetology written examination (typical vendor)?', 'Pearson VUE / NIC (per candidate handbook)', 'Internal school-only exams with no outside vendor', 'County health departments only', 'U.S. Department of Education directly', 'A', 'Candidates in Florida schedule through Pearson VUE / NIC (per candidate handbook) unless the board publishes a change—verify https://www.myfloridalicense.com/DBPR/cosmetology/.', 'https://www.myfloridalicense.com/DBPR/cosmetology/', 5),
  ('30000004-4000-8000-000000000004'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'What is the minimum passing score on the Florida cosmetology written exam (published target)?', '75%', '50%', '90%', '100% — any missed question fails', 'A', 'Florida sets a passing standard of 75% on the written portion for this license class.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 5),
  ('30000005-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'flashcard', 'state_law', 3, 'In Florida, cosmetology rules are found in Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'true', 'State law for Florida cosmetology is anchored in Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 4),
  ('30000006-4000-8000-000000000006'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'flashcard', 'state_law', 3, 'A Florida cosmetology candidate may ignore Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation (DBPR), Board of Cosmetology sanitation rules if their salon has private insurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'Licensure and inspection standards from Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation (DBPR), Board of Cosmetology apply regardless of private insurance.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 4),
  ('30000007-4000-8000-000000000007'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 3, 'After a Florida salon service, multi-use metal implements must be:', 'Cleaned, then disinfected per EPA-registered label instructions', 'Rinsed in plain water only', 'Wiped with a dry towel only', 'Stored without cleaning until the next client', 'A', 'Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation (DBPR), Board of Cosmetology expects infection control consistent with Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II and CDC best practices.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 5),
  ('30000008-4000-8000-000000000008'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 4, 'Blood on a workstation during a Florida service requires:', 'Stop service, glove up, clean with appropriate bloodborne pathogen protocol', 'Continue service if the client says it is fine', 'Cover with a cape and proceed', 'Wait until closing to disinfect', 'A', 'Bloodborne exposure procedures are enforced under Florida cosmetology sanitation rules.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 5),
  ('30000009-4000-8000-000000000009'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'true_false', 'sanitation', 3, 'Single-use porous items in Florida salons may be reused if they look clean.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'Porous single-use supplies must be discarded after one client.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 4),
  ('30000010-4000-8000-000000000010'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'anatomy', 2, 'The outermost layer of skin primarily responsible for barrier protection is the:', 'Epidermis', 'Dermis', 'Subcutaneous tissue', 'Matrix', 'A', 'Epidermis is the protective outer layer tested on national and state theory exams.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Skin Structure', 4),
  ('30000011-4000-8000-000000000011'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'anatomy', 2, 'Hair grows from the:', 'Hair follicle / dermal papilla', 'Epidermis only', 'Stratum corneum', 'Arrector pili exclusively', 'A', 'Active growth originates in the follicle at the dermal papilla.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Hair Structure', 4),
  ('30000012-4000-8000-000000000012'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'chemistry', 3, 'On the level system, level 7 represents:', 'Medium blonde depth', 'Black', 'Lightest blonde only', 'Red only', 'A', 'Level 7 is medium blonde on the 1–10 depth scale.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Haircolor', 4),
  ('30000013-4000-8000-000000000013'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'chemistry', 3, '20-volume developer is commonly used in Florida salons to:', 'Deposit on previously colored hair and lift up to ~2 levels on virgin hair', 'Guarantee 5 levels of lift on every scalp application', 'Replace disinfectant solutions', 'Neutralize relaxers without testing', 'A', '20-volume is standard deposit/slight-lift developer; always follow manufacturer and state scope.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 4),
  ('30000014-4000-8000-000000000014'::uuid, 'e3000001-0003-4003-8003-000000000003'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'practical', 3, 'Before chemical services in Florida, a required safety step is:', 'Consultation and patch test when manufacturer or state rules require', 'Skipping consultation for returning clients', 'Applying highest volume developer first', 'Mixing unrelated brands for speed', 'A', 'Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation (DBPR), Board of Cosmetology expects documented consultations; patch tests protect clients and licensees.', 'Florida Statutes Chapter 477, Part II', 5),
