  ('40000001-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 2, 'Which agency licenses cosmetologists in New York?', 'NY Department of State, Division of Licensing Services', 'U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA)', 'Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)', 'Federal Trade Commission (FTC)', 'A', 'NY Department of State, Division of Licensing Services regulates cosmetology licensure in New York.', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 5),
  ('40000002-4000-8000-000000000002'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'How many clock hours of training are required for a New York cosmetology operator license (current rule)?', '1000 hours', '1600 hours', '1200 hours', '1250 hours', 'A', 'New York requires 1000 training hours for the cosmetology pathway cited in NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement).', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 5),
  ('40000003-4000-8000-000000000003'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'Who administers the New York cosmetology written examination (typical vendor)?', 'Pearson VUE / PSI (per DOS scheduling)', 'Internal school-only exams with no outside vendor', 'County health departments only', 'U.S. Department of Education directly', 'A', 'Candidates in New York schedule through Pearson VUE / PSI (per DOS scheduling) unless the board publishes a change—verify https://dos.ny.gov/appearance-enhancement.', 'https://dos.ny.gov/appearance-enhancement', 5),
  ('40000004-4000-8000-000000000004'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'What is the minimum passing score on the New York cosmetology written exam (published target)?', '70%', '50%', '90%', '100% — any missed question fails', 'A', 'New York sets a passing standard of 70% on the written portion for this license class.', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 5),
  ('40000005-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'flashcard', 'state_law', 3, 'In New York, cosmetology rules are found in NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'true', 'State law for New York cosmetology is anchored in NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement).', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 4),
  ('40000006-4000-8000-000000000006'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'flashcard', 'state_law', 3, 'A New York cosmetology candidate may ignore NY Department of State, Division of Licensing Services sanitation rules if their salon has private insurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'Licensure and inspection standards from NY Department of State, Division of Licensing Services apply regardless of private insurance.', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 4),
  ('40000007-4000-8000-000000000007'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 3, 'After a New York salon service, multi-use metal implements must be:', 'Cleaned, then disinfected per EPA-registered label instructions', 'Rinsed in plain water only', 'Wiped with a dry towel only', 'Stored without cleaning until the next client', 'A', 'NY Department of State, Division of Licensing Services expects infection control consistent with NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement) and CDC best practices.', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 5),
  ('40000008-4000-8000-000000000008'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 4, 'Blood on a workstation during a New York service requires:', 'Stop service, glove up, clean with appropriate bloodborne pathogen protocol', 'Continue service if the client says it is fine', 'Cover with a cape and proceed', 'Wait until closing to disinfect', 'A', 'Bloodborne exposure procedures are enforced under New York cosmetology sanitation rules.', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 5),
  ('40000009-4000-8000-000000000009'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'true_false', 'sanitation', 3, 'Single-use porous items in New York salons may be reused if they look clean.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'Porous single-use supplies must be discarded after one client.', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 4),
  ('40000010-4000-8000-000000000010'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'anatomy', 2, 'The outermost layer of skin primarily responsible for barrier protection is the:', 'Epidermis', 'Dermis', 'Subcutaneous tissue', 'Matrix', 'A', 'Epidermis is the protective outer layer tested on national and state theory exams.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Skin Structure', 4),
  ('40000011-4000-8000-000000000011'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'anatomy', 2, 'Hair grows from the:', 'Hair follicle / dermal papilla', 'Epidermis only', 'Stratum corneum', 'Arrector pili exclusively', 'A', 'Active growth originates in the follicle at the dermal papilla.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Hair Structure', 4),
  ('40000012-4000-8000-000000000012'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'chemistry', 3, 'On the level system, level 7 represents:', 'Medium blonde depth', 'Black', 'Lightest blonde only', 'Red only', 'A', 'Level 7 is medium blonde on the 1–10 depth scale.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Haircolor', 4),
  ('40000013-4000-8000-000000000013'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'chemistry', 3, '20-volume developer is commonly used in New York salons to:', 'Deposit on previously colored hair and lift up to ~2 levels on virgin hair', 'Guarantee 5 levels of lift on every scalp application', 'Replace disinfectant solutions', 'Neutralize relaxers without testing', 'A', '20-volume is standard deposit/slight-lift developer; always follow manufacturer and state scope.', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 4),
  ('40000014-4000-8000-000000000014'::uuid, 'e4000001-0004-4004-8004-000000000004'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'practical', 3, 'Before chemical services in New York, a required safety step is:', 'Consultation and patch test when manufacturer or state rules require', 'Skipping consultation for returning clients', 'Applying highest volume developer first', 'Mixing unrelated brands for speed', 'A', 'NY Department of State, Division of Licensing Services expects documented consultations; patch tests protect clients and licensees.', 'NY General Business Law Article 27 (Appearance Enhancement)', 5),
