  ('50000001-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 2, 'Which agency licenses cosmetologists in Pennsylvania?', 'State Board of Cosmetology (PA Department of State)', 'U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA)', 'Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)', 'Federal Trade Commission (FTC)', 'A', 'State Board of Cosmetology (PA Department of State) regulates cosmetology licensure in Pennsylvania.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 5),
  ('50000002-4000-8000-000000000002'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'How many clock hours of training are required for a Pennsylvania cosmetology operator license (current rule)?', '1250 hours', '1000 hours', '1600 hours', '1200 hours', 'A', 'Pennsylvania requires 1250 training hours for the cosmetology pathway cited in 63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law).', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 5),
  ('50000003-4000-8000-000000000003'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'Who administers the Pennsylvania cosmetology written examination (typical vendor)?', 'Pearson VUE', 'Internal school-only exams with no outside vendor', 'County health departments only', 'U.S. Department of Education directly', 'A', 'Candidates in Pennsylvania schedule through Pearson VUE unless the board publishes a change—verify https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dos/programs-and-services/professional-licensing/cosmetology.html.', 'https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dos/programs-and-services/professional-licensing/cosmetology.html', 5),
  ('50000004-4000-8000-000000000004'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'state_law', 3, 'What is the minimum passing score on the Pennsylvania cosmetology written exam (published target)?', '75%', '50%', '90%', '100% — any missed question fails', 'A', 'Pennsylvania sets a passing standard of 75% on the written portion for this license class.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 5),
  ('50000005-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'flashcard', 'state_law', 3, 'In Pennsylvania, cosmetology rules are found in 63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'true', 'State law for Pennsylvania cosmetology is anchored in 63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law).', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 4),
  ('50000006-4000-8000-000000000006'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'flashcard', 'state_law', 3, 'A Pennsylvania cosmetology candidate may ignore State Board of Cosmetology (PA Department of State) sanitation rules if their salon has private insurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'Licensure and inspection standards from State Board of Cosmetology (PA Department of State) apply regardless of private insurance.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 4),
  ('50000007-4000-8000-000000000007'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 3, 'After a Pennsylvania salon service, multi-use metal implements must be:', 'Cleaned, then disinfected per EPA-registered label instructions', 'Rinsed in plain water only', 'Wiped with a dry towel only', 'Stored without cleaning until the next client', 'A', 'State Board of Cosmetology (PA Department of State) expects infection control consistent with 63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law) and CDC best practices.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 5),
  ('50000008-4000-8000-000000000008'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 4, 'Blood on a workstation during a Pennsylvania service requires:', 'Stop service, glove up, clean with appropriate bloodborne pathogen protocol', 'Continue service if the client says it is fine', 'Cover with a cape and proceed', 'Wait until closing to disinfect', 'A', 'Bloodborne exposure procedures are enforced under Pennsylvania cosmetology sanitation rules.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 5),
  ('50000009-4000-8000-000000000009'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'true_false', 'sanitation', 3, 'Single-use porous items in Pennsylvania salons may be reused if they look clean.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'false', 'Porous single-use supplies must be discarded after one client.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 4),
  ('50000010-4000-8000-000000000010'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'anatomy', 2, 'The outermost layer of skin primarily responsible for barrier protection is the:', 'Epidermis', 'Dermis', 'Subcutaneous tissue', 'Matrix', 'A', 'Epidermis is the protective outer layer tested on national and state theory exams.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Skin Structure', 4),
  ('50000011-4000-8000-000000000011'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'anatomy', 2, 'Hair grows from the:', 'Hair follicle / dermal papilla', 'Epidermis only', 'Stratum corneum', 'Arrector pili exclusively', 'A', 'Active growth originates in the follicle at the dermal papilla.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Hair Structure', 4),
  ('50000012-4000-8000-000000000012'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'chemistry', 3, 'On the level system, level 7 represents:', 'Medium blonde depth', 'Black', 'Lightest blonde only', 'Red only', 'A', 'Level 7 is medium blonde on the 1–10 depth scale.', 'Milady Standard Cosmetology — Haircolor', 4),
  ('50000013-4000-8000-000000000013'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'chemistry', 3, '20-volume developer is commonly used in Pennsylvania salons to:', 'Deposit on previously colored hair and lift up to ~2 levels on virgin hair', 'Guarantee 5 levels of lift on every scalp application', 'Replace disinfectant solutions', 'Neutralize relaxers without testing', 'A', '20-volume is standard deposit/slight-lift developer; always follow manufacturer and state scope.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 4),
  ('50000014-4000-8000-000000000014'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'practical', 3, 'Before chemical services in Pennsylvania, a required safety step is:', 'Consultation and patch test when manufacturer or state rules require', 'Skipping consultation for returning clients', 'Applying highest volume developer first', 'Mixing unrelated brands for speed', 'A', 'State Board of Cosmetology (PA Department of State) expects documented consultations; patch tests protect clients and licensees.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 5),
  ('50000015-4000-8000-000000000015'::uuid, 'e5000001-0005-4005-8005-000000000005'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'sanitation', 3, '[PA-1] EPA-registered disinfectants in Pennsylvania must be used:', 'According to the product label after pre-cleaning tools', 'Without pre-cleaning to save time', 'Only on porous single-use items', 'Only when a client requests it', 'A', 'Label contact times are enforceable under Pennsylvania sanitation statutes.', '63 P.S. §§ 531–551 (Cosmetology Law)', 4),
